## 4. Find First and Last Position of Element in Sorted Array – LeetCode #34

**Difficulty:** Medium

**Concept:** Apply Binary Search twice to find the first and last positions of the target.

**Time Complexity:** O(log n)  
**Space Complexity:** O(1)

```java
class Solution {
    public int[] searchRange(int[] nums, int target) {
        int first = findPosition(nums, target, true);
        int last = findPosition(nums, target, false);

        return new int[]{first, last};
    }

    private int findPosition(int[] nums, int target, boolean findFirst) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = nums.length - 1;
        int answer = -1;

        while (left <= right) {
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            if (nums[mid] == target) {
                answer = mid;

                if (findFirst) {
                    right = mid - 1;
                } else {
                    left = mid + 1;
                }
            } else if (nums[mid] < target) {
                left = mid + 1;
            } else {
                right = mid - 1;
            }
        }

        return answer;
    }
}
```

